@startuml
title Figure 2a — UML Package diagram — Spring Modulith application modules
top to bottom direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45

package "dev.specgraph.reference.identity\n<<application module>>" as Identity
package "dev.specgraph.reference.risk\n<<application module>>" as Risk
package "dev.specgraph.reference.customer\n<<application module>>" as Customer {
  package "customer.web\n<<inbound adapter package>>" as CustomerWeb
  package "customer.persistence\n<<outbound adapter package>>" as CustomerPersistence
}
package "dev.specgraph.reference.analysis\n<<application module>>" as Analysis
package "dev.specgraph.reference.demo\n<<application module>>" as Demo {
  package "demo.web\n<<inbound adapter package>>" as DemoWeb
  package "demo.persistence\n<<outbound adapter package>>" as DemoPersistence
}

Identity -[hidden]down-> Risk
Risk -[hidden]down-> Customer
Customer -[hidden]down-> Analysis
Analysis -[hidden]down-> Demo

Customer ..> Risk : public RiskEvidence contract
Analysis ..> Customer : customer/activity application contracts
Demo ..> Customer : generated customer/activity contracts
Demo ..> Risk : generated risk-evidence contracts

note right of CustomerWeb
  HTTP adapter is internal to the
  customer application module.
end note

note right of CustomerPersistence
  Synthetic/JPA persistence adapters
  provide CustomerActivityPort here.
end note

note right of DemoWeb
  Opt-in scenario generation is exposed
  through the demo module boundary.
end note

note right of DemoPersistence
  Replayable generated evidence is
  materialized behind the demo-owned port.
end note

note bottom
  UML Package diagram: the five direct packages are the actual Spring Modulith module
  bases. Adapter sub-packages remain inside their owning module. Detailed hexagonal
  Adapter/Strategy/Facade roles are shown in the component/port views rather than by
  inventing package-per-layer namespaces that do not exist in the implementation.
  Architecture verification ratchets the exact module identifiers:
  identity, customer, risk, analysis, demo.
end note
@enduml
